## Bibliography
- refs/discipline.bib  — all chapters (core PGx, ML, opioid epidemic, APCD, XAI)
- refs/bmic-jpm.bib    — CH_1, CH_5 (MDPI JPM-specific)
- refs/cpt-psp.bib     — CH_2, CH_4 (CPT:PSP-specific)
- refs/cts.bib         — CH_3 (CTS-specific)
- Zotero workflow: refs/README.md
- NEVER use underscores in .bib filenames — LaTeX escapes _ in .aux files

## Citation Formatting
- In .qmd files: always use [@key] Pandoc syntax (never \citep{} directly)
- PDF (natbib): Quarto converts [@key] → \citep{key} automatically
- Docx (citeproc): uses templates/csl/ama.csl (Wiley) or templates/csl/mdpi.csl (MDPI)
- cite-method: natbib is set in all chapter YAML

## CSL Files
- templates/csl/ama.csl   — CH_2, CH_3, CH_4, CH_6 (AMA numbered superscript)
- templates/csl/mdpi.csl  — CH_1, CH_5 (MDPI numbered)

## Template Rules
- MDPI chapters (CH_1, CH_5): use pdf: format block + template: override
- Wiley chapters (CH_2, CH_3, CH_4): use wiley-njd-pdf: format block + template: override
- Never use --to pdf for Wiley chapters — must use --to wiley-njd-pdf
- WileyNJDv5 class (not deprecated WileyNJD-v2)
- Extension path: _extensions/ramiromagno/wiley-njd/

## YAML Reserved Fields (renamed to avoid Quarto conflicts)
- journal:       → target-journal:
- abbreviations: → manuscript-abbreviations:
- articletype:   → target-articletype:
- biblio-style:  REMOVED from CH_1/CH_5 (mdpi.cls sets it internally)

## LaTeX Compatibility Shims (already applied — do not remove)
- \providecommand{\tightlist}{...} in all templates
- \let\listoflistings\relax before $header-includes$
- \usepackage{calc} for \real{} in Pandoc longtable column widths
- longtable 2-column patch in cpt_psp_template.tex (STIX2COL layout)

## Key Content Rules
- All placeholder text uses [BRACKET] format: [N = XX,XXX], [IRB-XXXX], etc.
- Inline math: never write $\cmd$digit — digit immediately after $ breaks Quarto parser
  Correct: ${\sim}1.2$ M   Wrong: $\sim$1.2 M
- Figures live in figures/chXX/ — filenames must match QMD references exactly
- Placeholder PDFs are in figures/ until real pipeline outputs replace them

## Placeholder Tracker (fill from pipeline outputs)
- [CRD-XXXXXX]         CH_1    PROSPERO registration
- [IRB-XXXX]           CH_2–5  VCU IRB waiver number
- [N = XX,XXX]         CH_2–5  2_create_cohort/outputs/
- [0.XX ± 0.XX] AUROC  CH_3–4  6_final_model/outputs/
- [top drug/code]      CH_3–4  7_shap_analysis/outputs/
- [XX synergistic pairs] CH_4  8_ffa_analysis/outputs/
- < 500 ms cold-start  CH_5    Lambda CloudWatch logs
- figures/chXX/*.pdf   All     9_dashboard_visuals/
- [Funding statement]  All     Grant number + funder
- [Department Name]    CH_1    VCU department name
- Author contributions All     CRediT taxonomy (required by MDPI + Wiley)
- Data availability    All     VCHI DUA restricts public deposit

## File Naming Conventions
- .bib files: hyphens not underscores (bmic-jpm.bib, cpt-psp.bib, cts.bib)
- Output PDFs: ch01_bmic_jpm.pdf, ch02_psp.pdf, ch03_cts.pdf, ch04_psp.pdf,
               ch05_bmic_jpm.pdf, ch06_conclusion.pdf
- Docx drafts: ch0X_*_draft.docx → edits/

## .gitignore Notes
- output/*.pdf and edits/*.docx are excluded (generated artifacts)
- CH_*/*.tex, *.aux, *.bbl, *.blg, *.log, *.out, *.toc excluded
- CH_*/*.cls, *.sty, *.bst, Fonts/ excluded (Wiley extension copies these during build)
